{
    "background_story": "Mohammad was a humble bridge player from a small village. He spent most of his evenings at the local community center, teaching the intricacies of the game to newcomers. His favorite convention was the Stayman, a complex bid that required precision and strategy. Mohammad's mastery of the Stayman led to numerous tournament victories, earning him a reputation as a bridge virtuoso. However, his true legacy lay in his patience and kindness towards his students. He spent countless hours explaining the Stayman to anyone willing to learn, never growing tired of the question 'what if...'. As a result, Mohammad's village produced an impressive number of skilled bridge players, all of whom credited their success to his dedication and expertise. His love for the game, particularly the Stayman, inspired a generation of players to stay and master the art of bridge.",
